    // Raw glk image_draw_scaled(win, image, val1, val2, width, height). `image` is a resource id
    // and `val1` is polymorphic — x for a graphics window, an alignment (eGlulxImageAlign) for a
    // text-buffer window — so both are `var`: this keeps the low-level opcode from depending on the
    // blorb-gated `eAssets`/`eGlulxImageAlign` types (which would break a non-blorb Glulx build) and
    // lets every caller pass its own type. Semantics live in the facades (printRules.img, window draw).
    emitter int imageDrawScaled(int win, var img, var alignOrX, int y, int width, int height){
        __glkHook(226, $win, $img, $alignOrX, $y, $width, $height)
    }

